---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How this site uses Google Analytics, hosting logs, browser storage, and contact email.">
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-5 px-4 pt-10 pb-10 md:px-20 md:pt-18 md:pb-18">
    <div class="text-lg">
      <p class="text-dim">$ cat ~/privacy.md</p>
      <h1 class="font-semibold text-3xl">Privacy</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose max-w-prose">
      <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-09-20">20 September 2026</time>.</p>
      <p>
        I’m {site.name}, the owner of this personal site, based in Armenia. This page explains how information is handled
        when you visit {new URL(site.url).hostname} or contact me. The site has no ads, forms, or accounts.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site uses Google Analytics to understand visits and which pages people read. The Google tag
        loads when you visit. It is configured with <code>analytics_storage</code> set to
        <code>denied</code>, which prevents it from reading or writing first-party analytics cookies.
        This setting does not stop data from being sent to Google.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google receives measurements without analytics cookies. These can include the page URL
        (including query parameters), referrer, time of the visit, browser and device information,
        consent settings, and a random number generated for each page load. Google also receives your
        IP address as part of the connection and can use it to estimate your location, including your
        city. Collection of detailed device information is enabled.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google signals and user-provided data collection are disabled, and the site does not use
        User-ID. No advertising products are linked to this Analytics property. Search Console is
        linked to show how people find the site through Google Search.
      </p>
      <p>
        Optional sharing for Google products and services is disabled. Sharing for modeling
        contributions and business insights is enabled, which allows Google to combine data into
        statistics with data from other sites and apps. Google also has permission to access account
        data for technical support and business recommendations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Google Analytics property’s data retention setting is 14 months. This setting applies to
        the user and event data covered by Google’s retention controls. It does not set a deletion
        deadline for standard aggregated reports.
      </p>
      <p>
        See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>
        and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a> for details about
        its processing, retention, and international data transfers. You can prevent this site’s
        analytics script from running by disabling JavaScript for this site in your browser.
      </p>
      <h2>Browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        If you change the single-key shortcuts setting in the keyboard help, the site saves your
        choice in your browser’s local storage under <code>shortcuts</code>. The value is
        <code>on</code> or <code>off</code>. The site does not send this value to a server. It has no
        expiry set by the site. You can remove it by clearing this site’s data in your browser.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub Pages hosts this site. GitHub collects visitors’ IP addresses in logs for security.
        Its handling of this information is described in the
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Email and privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        The email links open your email app. If you send me a message, I receive your email address,
        the message, and any information you include. Your email provider and mine process the email
        to deliver it. I keep correspondence for as long as needed for the purpose of the exchange.
      </p>
      <p>
        For questions about this page or requests about your personal information, contact
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        External links, including social and sharing links, take you to other sites. Their privacy
        policies apply when you visit them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
